## 1. MIDI processing

Midi messages have attributes that are selective and dependent on other attributes
B field exist only if A is present kind of things
Beware of this.


## 2. making a wave

define sampling rate: how many samples per second
define duration (in seconds)
sampling rate x duration  --> how many samples, n
make a tensor that generates this: [0, ... , n -1] where n is the number of samples

divide each number above by sr ...
[0 ... 1, 1.1 ... 2, ... 3, ... duration] = [0 1/16000, 2/16000, ... 16000/16000, ... , n_sec * 16000/16000]
--> time elapsed

first part (0, 1/16000, ... , 16000/16000) is one sec and contains e.g. 440 sine waves
--> 다시 다른 resolution 으로 나타내면, (0, ..., 1/440, ..., 2/440, .... , 440/440)
want to scale this such that
 0 --> 0
 1/440 sec --> ((16000/440) / 16000) 초 --> 2 pi   *** 16000/440 16000 sample 안에 440 개의 sine wave 있고, 하나의 sine wave 마다 몇초에 해당하는가 ...
 2/440 --> ((16000/440 * 2) / 16000) 초 --> 4 pi
 440/440 --> ((16000/440 * 440) /16000) --> 880 pi
 must multiply 440 * 2 pi 로 scale 해야 한다

--- 
more flexible wave with varied frequency ... 시간에 따라 freq 변하는 상황

make a tensor that shows the varied frequency:
 like [440 442 450 440 250 ...] --> must be above zero ... !!! 그냥 보통 sine 하면 -1 1 사이 ... give it an offset to make it above zero and not make and error

sr = 16000 wave 는 이렇게 시간이 흐를 것 [0 1/16000 2/16000 ...]

take each value one at a time, 
e.g. 1 inc /16000 일 때 440 frequency wave --> compute proportion of time for 1 inc 440 wave --> 440 * 1/16000 
2 inc /16000 일 때 442 frequency wave --> compute proportion of (so far) = 442 * 2/16000    
3 inc / 16000 일 때 450 --> compute proportion of (so far) for 450 = 450 * 3/16000

see the code too


